id: focal
name: Focal
kind: crafting
categories: weights
slots: 1
# "Upon creating this piece of Apparel, select either your Strike or Dodge Rolls."
choices: strike=Strike Rolls, dodge=Dodge Rolls
# The chosen one is all the Weights Category reaches - its penalty, and its Doff Bonus.
narrowsCategory: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Strike or Dodge, chosen when it is made: the only Combat Roll the Weights lower, and the only
  one its Doff Bonus raises.
# What it does, for the Effects on its Item's sheet: one line to an effect, each opening with
# its tag as the rulebook writes one - [Passive], [Automatic, 1/Encounter].
summary: >
  [Passive]: The chosen Combat Roll is the only one the Weights lower, and the only one this
  piece's Doff Bonus raises.
text: >
  Focal: Designed to improve a single aspect of combat, these weights aren’t as heavy, but are
  placed on specific areas of the body.
  –Apparel Category: Weights
  –Prerequisites: N/A
  –Quality Slots: 1
  –Effects: Upon creating this piece of Apparel, select either your Strike or Dodge Rolls. The
  chosen Combat Roll is the only Combat Roll reduced by the effects of the Weight Apparel
  Category, but only that Combat Roll benefits from this piece of Apparel’s Doff Bonus.

---

# --- What is built -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The choice: Strike or Dodge, asked when it is added and shown on its row.
#
# --- What is not built ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# What it changes is the Weights Category's own effects and the Doff Bonus, and both come with
# the rest of the Apparel rules. They read the choice through narrowedRoll() in module/gear.mjs.
